{:edb/db-before-t 1386 :edb/db-after-t 1387 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534699 50 #inst "2026-10-08T04:31:47.048Z" 13194139534699 true] [17592186105516 1100 "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 2,-3,2 \\rangle$, $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle -1,0,5 \\rangle$, and $\\mathbf{c}=\\langle 1,2,3 \\rangle$. Find $\\mathbf{a} \\cdot (\\mathbf{b} \\times \\mathbf{c})$." 13194139534699 false] [17592186105516 1100 "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 2,-3,2 \\rangle,$ $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle -1,0,5 \\rangle,$ and $\\mathbf{c}=\\langle 1,2,3 \\rangle.$ Find $\\mathbf{a} \\cdot (\\mathbf{b} \\times \\mathbf{c}).$" 13194139534699 true] [17592186105516 1145 "First, we find the cross product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b\\times c & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(0\\cdot 3-5\\cdot 2)i-(-1\\cdot 3-5\\cdot 1)j+(-1\\cdot 2-0\\cdot 2)k \\\\  & =-10i+8j-2k \\\\  & =⟨-10,8,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the scalar triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =⟨2,-3,2⟩\\cdot ⟨-10,8,-2⟩ \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-10)+(-3)\\cdot 8+2\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =-48\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534699 true] [17592186105516 1145 "First, we find the cross product:\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}\\mathbf{b} \\times  \\mathbf{c} & = \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{ccc}\\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ - 1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{array}\\right\\vert \\\\  & = \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{cc}0 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{array}\\right\\vert \\mathbf{i} - \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{cc}- 1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right\\vert \\mathbf{j} + \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{cc}- 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right\\vert \\mathbf{k} \\\\  & = ( 0 \\cdot  3 - 5 \\cdot  2 ) \\mathbf{i} - ( - 1 \\cdot  3 - 5 \\cdot  1 ) \\mathbf{j} + ( - 1 \\cdot  2 - 0 \\cdot  2 ) \\mathbf{k} \\\\  & = - 10 \\mathbf{i} + 8 \\mathbf{j} - 2 \\mathbf{k} \\\\  & = \\langle  - 10 , 8 , - 2 \\rangle\\end{array}$$\n\nNow, we can compute the scalar triple product:\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}\\mathbf{a} \\cdot  ( \\mathbf{b} \\times  \\mathbf{c} ) & = \\langle  2 , - 3 , 2 \\rangle  \\cdot  \\langle  - 10 , 8 , - 2 \\rangle \\\\  & = 2 \\cdot  ( - 10 ) + ( - 3 ) \\cdot  8 + 2 \\cdot  ( - 2 ) \\\\  & = - 48\\end{array}$$" 13194139534699 false] [17592186105517 1100 "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 4,2,-1 \\rangle$, $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 0,2,1 \\rangle$, and $\\mathbf{c}=\\langle -1,-1,2 \\rangle$. Find $\\mathbf{a} \\cdot (\\mathbf{b} \\times \\mathbf{c})$." 13194139534699 false] [17592186105517 1100 "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 4,2,-1 \\rangle,$ $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 0,2,1 \\rangle,$ and $\\mathbf{c}=\\langle -1,-1,2 \\rangle.$ Find $\\mathbf{a} \\cdot (\\mathbf{b} \\times \\mathbf{c}).$" 13194139534699 true] [17592186105517 1145 "Remember that the scalar triple product $\\mathbf{a} \\cdot (\\mathbf{b} \\times \\mathbf{c})$ is just the determinant of the matrix whose rows are given by $\\mathbf{a}$, $\\mathbf{b}$, and $\\mathbf{c}$.\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}\\mathbf{a} \\cdot  ( \\mathbf{b} \\times  \\mathbf{c} ) & = \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{ccc}4 & 2 & - 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ - 1 & - 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right\\vert \\\\  & = 4 \\cdot  \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{cc}2 & 1 \\\\ - 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right\\vert - 2 \\cdot  \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{cc}0 & 1 \\\\ - 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right\\vert + ( - 1 ) \\cdot  \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{cc}0 & 2 \\\\ - 1 & - 1\\end{array}\\right\\vert \\\\  & = 4 \\cdot  ( 2 \\cdot  2 - 1 \\cdot  ( - 1 ) ) - 2 \\cdot  ( 0 \\cdot  2 - 1 \\cdot  ( - 1 ) ) + ( - 1 ) \\cdot  ( 0 \\cdot  ( - 1 ) - 2 \\cdot  ( - 1 ) ) \\\\  & = 20 - 2 - 2 \\\\  & = 16.\\end{array}$$" 13194139534699 false] [17592186105517 1145 "Remember that the scalar triple product $\\mathbf{a} \\cdot (\\mathbf{b} \\times \\mathbf{c})$ is just the determinant of the matrix whose rows are given by $\\mathbf{a},$ $\\mathbf{b},$ and $\\mathbf{c}.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|+(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4\\cdot (2\\cdot 2-1\\cdot (-1))-2\\cdot (0\\cdot 2-1\\cdot (-1))+(-1)\\cdot (0\\cdot (-1)-2\\cdot (-1)) \\\\  & =20-2-2 \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534699 true] [17592186105518 1100 "Find $\\mathbf{c} \\cdot (\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b})$, if $2\\mathbf{a} \\cdot (\\mathbf{b} \\times 3\\mathbf{c}) = 5$." 13194139534699 false] [17592186105518 1100 "Find $\\mathbf{c} \\cdot (\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}),$ if $2\\mathbf{a} \\cdot (\\mathbf{b} \\times 3\\mathbf{c}) = 5.$" 13194139534699 true] [17592186105518 1145 "First, we factor out the constants and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2a\\cdot (b\\times 3c) & =5 \\\\ 2\\cdot [a\\cdot (b\\times 3c)] & =5 \\\\ 2\\cdot 3\\cdot [a\\cdot (b\\times c)] & =5 \\\\ a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =\\frac{5}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we swap $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{c}$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c\\cdot (b\\times a) & =-\\frac{5}{6},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand again we swap $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c\\cdot (a\\times b) & =\\frac{5}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534699 true] [17592186105518 1145 "First, we factor out the constants and get\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}2 \\mathbf{a} \\cdot  ( \\mathbf{b} \\times  3 \\mathbf{c} ) & = 5 \\\\ 2 \\cdot  [ \\mathbf{a} \\cdot  ( \\mathbf{b} \\times  3 \\mathbf{c} ) ] & = 5 \\\\ 2 \\cdot  3 \\cdot  [ \\mathbf{a} \\cdot  ( \\mathbf{b} \\times  \\mathbf{c} ) ] & = 5 \\\\ \\mathbf{a} \\cdot  ( \\mathbf{b} \\times  \\mathbf{c} ) & = \\frac{5}{6} .\\end{array}$$\n\nThen, we swap $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{c}$ to get\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}\\mathbf{c} \\cdot  ( \\mathbf{b} \\times  \\mathb